  "notes": {
    "fA": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Foundations", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 7520, "page": "foundations"},
    "fB": {"x": 0, "y": 6140, "text": "Shared chrome", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 1240, "page": "foundations"},
    "fC": {"x": 1320, "y": 6140, "text": "Dark mode", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 1240, "page": "foundations"},
    "fN": {"x": -560, "y": 0, "w": 440, "text": "How this canvas works\n\n• Tokens and every component class live in one shared stylesheet, project/gebeya.css. Change a token there and every artboard follows.\n• Every screen is one responsive page: the 360 px frame and the desktop frame render the same file (desktop frames import the phone file at 1280 px).\n• Every screen has a Theme tweak (light / dark); most have a state tweak too (out of stock, unverified, empty, errors, notices).\n• Look: Apple-like restraint. White and near-black do most of the work; one green accent marks links, focus, progress and buyer protection.", "page": "foundations"},
    "fQ": {"x": -560, "y": 700, "w": 440, "text": "Brief coverage\n\n• §3 constraints: 360 px first, no sideways scroll, EN + AM, light + dark, plain form posts, ETB / ብር money, 44 px targets, visible labels, status in words.\n• §5 screens: every public, auth, buyer and seller screen at 360 px and desktop, plus the states the brief lists.\n• §9 components: all 21 with their states, on the two component boards (light and dark).\n• §10: tokens, component specs, Amharic for checkout, both order pages, wallet and product editor, and these flow notes.", "page": "foundations"},

    "bA": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Buyer flow · phone", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3000, "page": "buyer"},
    "bB": {"x": 0, "y": 2300, "text": "Buyer states · phone", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3880, "page": "buyer"},
    "bC": {"x": 0, "y": 5280, "text": "Buyer · desktop", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 9440, "page": "buyer"},
    "bN": {"x": -560, "y": 0, "w": 440, "text": "Flow notes · buyer\n\n• Product link: price, options, quantity and Buy now come first; the protection block sits right under the buttons. The gallery swipes on phone; thumbnails are plain #anchors, so it works without JavaScript.\n• Header on phone: guests always see Log in. Signed-in links (My orders, My shop) move into a menu built on <details>. Log out stays in the footer.\n• Checkout: saved addresses and the note belong to the pay form via the form attribute, so “Add a new address” is its own form (Save address) without nesting. Tweaks show every error from the brief and the busy pay button that stops double orders.\n• Report a problem is a <details> disclosure with Open dispute and Cancel; it posts without JavaScript.\n• No action from the brief was removed.", "page": "buyer"},

    "sA": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Seller flow · phone", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3880, "page": "seller"},
    "sB": {"x": 0, "y": 3060, "text": "Seller states", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 1680, "page": "seller"},
    "sC": {"x": 0, "y": 5540, "text": "Seller · desktop", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 12160, "page": "seller"},
    "sN": {"x": -560, "y": 0, "w": 440, "text": "Flow notes · seller\n\n• Seller tabs: a five-up segmented bar under the header on phone (fits 360 px in English and Amharic); a left sidebar on desktop.\n• Product editor is split into cards (Share, Options, Details, Images, Delete). Each option has three small forms — Save, Set stock, Hide/Remove — so every action is its own submit and reports back at the top.\n• Products list shows a thumbnail and price per row. The brief says the list API doesn’t return these yet — this needs a backend change, or drop them.\n• Cancel and refund buyer and Delete product sit behind a <details> confirmation.\n• No action from the brief was removed.", "page": "seller"},

    "aA": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Public & auth · phone", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3440, "page": "auth"},
    "aB": {"x": 0, "y": 1860, "text": "Public & auth · desktop", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 8080, "page": "auth"},
    "aN": {"x": -560, "y": 0, "w": 440, "text": "Flow notes · auth\n\n• Verify phone uses one code field with autocomplete=\"one-time-code\" so Android fills it from the SMS. State tweak: not sent / sent / wrong code / expired.\n• Reset password keeps two steps; the “we sent a code” message stays vague on purpose. Log in shows the “password changed” notice after step 2.\n• Desktop auth pages keep the same narrow column, centred.", "page": "auth"},

    "amA": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Amharic · አማርኛ", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2120, "page": "amharic"},
    "amN": {"x": -560, "y": 0, "w": 440, "text": "About the Amharic frames\n\n• Status labels and the tagline are taken from the brief.\n• All other Amharic copy is a draft written to test layout, because src/lib/i18n/am.ts could not be read. Swap in the real strings before hand-off.\n• Dates keep the English “22 Oct 2026, 13:37” format until am.ts says otherwise.\n• Ethiopic uses Noto Sans Ethiopic with taller line heights and no negative letter-spacing (see Tokens).", "page": "amharic"}
  },
  "designSystems": []
}
